From 42f0c03d79c0345e55f8eeb7975494067f8dc3da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kuasar Sandbox <noreply@kuasar.dev>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 17:13:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-devices: stage vsock reset before snapshot

Lazy restore can fault the virtqueue pages after device activation, so consuming an event descriptor while activating a restored vsock device is not reliable. Publish TRANSPORT_RESET while the source VM is paused for snapshot instead, persist the pending acknowledgement, and only re-signal the already-used event queue after restore.

Keep restored RX gated until the guest refills the event queue. Drain pre-snapshot kicks so stale epoll events cannot acknowledge the new reset, and leave ordinary pause/resume semantics unchanged.
